<!--
  RM_ShadeMite.xml                        RimMandrake — DUNESEA_SHADE_COMMENSAL_MICROFAUNA_1

  Resolves ledger slug "grain-scale commensal fauna riding RM_MirrorGiant's
  shade" (dune_sea.md §4: "the giants carry the only moving shadows on the
  planet, and there is an ecology living in them... commensals ride it,
  shelter under it, and follow it"; roster's own new_defs entry, "shade-
  commensal micro-fauna living under a walking giant", mechanic_load "C#:
  shade-follow (no donor mechanic keys to another creature's shadow)").

  Third consumer of the shared shade-follow mechanism — do not re-derive
  it. First consumer: RSW_GlitterBird follows RSW_ShadeWhale
  (DESERT_GLITTER_BIRDS_COMMENSALS_1). This is the second and final
  planned consumer named in that item's own build note: RM_MirrorGiant now
  carries RM_CompProperties_ShadowCaster (this same pass); this def is a
  RM_ShadowFollowerExtension-tagged commensal that follows whatever
  spawned pawn on the map carries that comp — it names no host by
  defName. searchRadius 60, same as the glitter-bird: RM_MirrorGiant is
  even rarer (wildAnimals commonality 0.0005 vs. the whale's 0.015), so a
  short search radius would make the follow behavior effectively never
  trigger on a real map.

  RM_-tier, not RUT_ or RSW_: invented content, no Star Wars flavor, per
  Q11a — belongs franchise-free in mandrake.rm.stillsand directly (same
  reasoning as RM_MirrorGiant/RM_DustHusk, authored this same wave), wired
  into RM_Stillsand_Biome.xml's own wildAnimals, not the frozen
  RUT_ExtremeDesert.xml twin and not WildAnimals_Stillsand.xml (that file
  only replays Star-Wars-named content copied off the twin).

  Body: grain-scale per dune_sea.md §4's bimodal law ("giants on the
  surface, and grain-scale life below it, with a hard gap where every
  ordinary animal would be") — bodySize 0.18, in the same band as
  RM_DustHusk (0.15, this same mod). Checked cast_assignment.csv/
  animal_census.csv first for an existing unclaimed grain-scale candidate
  before authoring from scratch (this item's own instruction); every
  grain-scale row there is already cast to RUT_ExtremeDesert (the frozen,
  Star-Wars-named twin) and none is free to reuse directly in the RM_
  tier without re-routing it through the IP patch layer, which this slug
  does not call for — so a new invented species is correct here, not a
  reuse. Same vanilla QuadrupedAnimalWithPawsAndTail body RM_DustHusk
  uses — no new BodyDef, no external dependency.

  Not a dormancy reskin (RM_DustHusk's own mechanic): this is an active
  follower, awake and moving whenever its host is on the map.

  Art: no existing render found for "shade mite"/"shadow mite"/
  "commensal"/"mirror giant" companion in
  infrastructure/artpipe/{done,pending,registry.jsonl} (checked this
  pass). One 3-facing job filed, rmshademite_v1_{south,east,north}.

  🔴 THE NAME IS NOT SETTLED — RM_ShadeMite is the INTERNAL working
  defName, same posture RM_Oommok/RM_Siidda used before their own naming.
  STILLSAND_RULED_CONTENT_1 (2026-09-27 sitting) ratified oommok/siidda and
  four filler coins (ruukka, oorrik, eemmok, vaalok — none of them this def)
  but did not name this creature; STILLSAND_SHIPPING_NAMES_1, which this
  comment used to cite, was never filed and does not exist in items/ or the
  ledger shards. This remains a genuinely unsettled name, most likely to be
  resolved alongside the roster fill-out commission's own coined names.
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="AnimalThingBase">
    <defName>RM_ShadeMite</defName>
    <label>shade mite</label>
    <description>A grain-scale scuttler that has never once, in its whole life, stood in direct sun. It lives entirely inside the moving shadow of a mirror giant — feeding on what the giant's bulk crushes into the sand, sheltering under the coolest ground on the planet, and moving only when the shadow moves. A shade mite separated from its giant does not go looking for another one; out here, there usually isn't another one to find.</description>
    <statBases>
      <MoveSpeed>2.2</MoveSpeed>
      <Mass>0.3</Mass>
      <MarketValue>10</MarketValue>
      <Wildness>0.9</Wildness>
      <ComfyTemperatureMin>-10</ComfyTemperatureMin>
      <ComfyTemperatureMax>999</ComfyTemperatureMax>
    </statBases>
    <tools>
      <li>
        <label>mandible</label>
        <capacities>
          <li>Bite</li>
        </capacities>
        <power>3</power>
        <cooldownTime>1.5</cooldownTime>
        <linkedBodyPartsGroup>Teeth</linkedBodyPartsGroup>
      </li>
    </tools>
    <modExtensions>
      <!-- DUNESEA_SHADE_COMMENSAL_MICROFAUNA_1's shade-follow mechanism —
           see this file's own header. -->
      <li Class="RimMandrake.CreatureBehaviors.RM_ShadowFollowerExtension">
        <searchRadius>60</searchRadius>
      </li>
    </modExtensions>
    <race>
      <body>QuadrupedAnimalWithPawsAndTail</body>
      <predator>false</predator>
      <herdAnimal>false</herdAnimal> <!-- bound to one host's shadow, not a flock -->
      <baseBodySize>0.18</baseBodySize>
      <baseHealthScale>0.35</baseHealthScale>
      <baseHungerRate>0.06</baseHungerRate>
      <foodType>OmnivoreRoughAnimal</foodType>
      <trainability>None</trainability>
      <roamMtbDays>60</roamMtbDays>
      <manhunterOnDamageChance>0</manhunterOnDamageChance>
      <manhunterOnTameFailChance>0</manhunterOnTameFailChance>
      <lifeExpectancy>10</lifeExpectancy>
      <gestationPeriodDays>5</gestationPeriodDays>
      <litterSizeCurve>
        <points>
          <li>(0.5, 0)</li>
          <li>(1, 1)</li>
          <li>(3, 0.5)</li>
          <li>(5, 0)</li>
        </points>
      </litterSizeCurve>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalBaby</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>0.08</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalAdult</def>
          <minAge>0.2</minAge>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
      <soundMeleeHitPawn>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitPawn</soundMeleeHitPawn>
      <soundMeleeHitBuilding>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_HitBuilding</soundMeleeHitBuilding>
      <soundMeleeMiss>Pawn_Melee_SmallScratch_Miss</soundMeleeMiss>
      <soundEating>Herbivore_Eat</soundEating>
    </race>
    <tradeTags>
      <li>AnimalExotic</li>
    </tradeTags>
  </ThingDef>

  <PawnKindDef ParentName="AnimalKindBase">
    <defName>RM_ShadeMite</defName>
    <label>shade mite</label>
    <labelPlural>shade mites</labelPlural>
    <race>RM_ShadeMite</race>
    <combatPower>3</combatPower>
    <wildGroupSize>2~5</wildGroupSize>
    <ecoSystemWeight>0.15</ecoSystemWeight>
    <lifeStages>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_ShadeMite/RM_ShadeMite</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.3</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_ShadeMite/RM_ShadeMite</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.4</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
      <li>
        <bodyGraphicData>
          <texPath>Things/Pawn/Animal/RM_ShadeMite/RM_ShadeMite</texPath>
          <graphicClass>Graphic_Multi</graphicClass>
          <drawSize>0.5</drawSize>
        </bodyGraphicData>
      </li>
    </lifeStages>
  </PawnKindDef>

</Defs>
